# Nothing here is currently blocking: every claim in the paper is sourced.
# The entries below record checks that came back empty, so that the same
# ground is not covered twice.
#
# Nine entries were removed from this file because no claim needed them:
# guidelines_mma_pa, epi_meta, biomarkers_review, natural_history_2012,
# grunert55, trial_challenges, mayo_nlp, mrna_moa, pathophys_treatment.
# A reference comes back when a claim requires it, not the other way round.
# residual_carboxylase  Claim that residual carboxylation in PCC-deficient
#                     cells derives from a DISTINCT carboxylase. Source not
#                     identified. NO LONGER NEEDED: the null-genotype anchor
#                     now rests on the structure of the model, under which any
#                     residual elimination is absorbed into k_e whatever its
#                     molecular origin. The claim is out of the paper.
# carrier_activity    Obligate carriers retain ~50% activity, asymptomatic.
#                     CHECKED and NOT FOUND. saudi84 does not discuss carrier
#                     activity. GeneReviews NBK92946 states that heterozygotes
#                     are asymptomatic but also that "fibroblast enzymatic
#                     analyses are not reliable for detection of
#                     heterozygotes", which undercuts the ~50% anchor rather
#                     than supporting it. The claim is out of the paper.
# nmd_frameshift      Frameshift variants with a premature termination codon
#                     are subject to nonsense-mediated decay. CHECKED: neither
#                     GeneReviews NBK92946 nor saudi84 states it. The claim is
#                     out of the paper; the anchor does not need it.
# saudi_carrier_top4  "PA among the four most frequent disorders in Saudi
#                     carrier screening". No source found. Out of the paper.

